---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PlannerCTA from '../../components/PlannerCTA.astro';
import SelectSaunasButton from '../../components/SelectSaunasButton.astro';

const harviaM3Url = 'https://selectsaunas.com/products/harvia-m3-wood-burning-sauna-stove';
const huumFlowMiniUrl = 'https://selectsaunas.com/products/huum';
const harviaLegendUrl = 'https://selectsaunas.com/products/harvia-legend-240-sl-21kw-wood-burning-sauna-stove-w-fire-chamber-extension';

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the best wood-burning sauna heater?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "There is no single best wood-burning heater. The right model must fit the manufacturer's calculated room range, required clearances, chimney system, loading location, stone load, and local approval requirements. The Harvia M3, HUUM HIVE Flow Mini, and Harvia Legend 240 SL represent three different project formats."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I size a wood-burning sauna heater?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Measure the finished interior volume and apply the selected manufacturer's adjustments for glass, masonry, log walls, and other uninsulated surfaces. Use the current manual for the exact model. Do not automatically oversize the heater."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does a wood sauna heater include the chimney and stones?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Often it does not. Confirm the stove, required stone type and quantity, chimney components, floor and wall protection, safety rail, flashing, and installation labor as separate line items before ordering."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---
<Base
  title="Best Wood-Burning Sauna Heaters? Compare 3 Current Formats"
  description="Compare the Harvia M3, HUUM HIVE Flow Mini, and Harvia Legend 240 SL by room range, loading format, stone amount, and installation scope."
  canonical="/guides/best-wood-burning-sauna-heaters"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <p class="text-sm text-amber-700 font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Wood heater buying guide</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-stone-900 leading-tight mb-4">Best wood-burning sauna heaters? Compare three current formats</h1>
      <p class="text-stone-500 text-sm">Last reviewed August 15, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden mb-8">
      <img src="/images/lifestyle/sauna-wood-stove-interior.jpg" alt="Wood-burning sauna stove installed beside wooden benches" class="w-full object-cover max-h-80" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800" />
    </div>

    <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-5 mb-8 text-sm text-stone-700">
      <strong>Research scope:</strong> This is a desk-researched comparison, not a hands-on test. We checked current manufacturer product data, North American manuals, listed room ranges, stone loads, loading formats, and authorized-retailer packages. We did not assign ratings or a universal winner.
    </div>

    <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 mb-4">A wood stove is part of a fire, chimney, ventilation, and clearance system. Choose the system first. Then choose the model whose current manual fits it.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-8">The three heaters below solve different problems. The Harvia M3 is a compact in-room-loading stove. The HUUM HIVE Flow Mini pairs a similar listed room range with a much larger stone mass. The Harvia Legend 240 SL serves larger rooms and loads from the other side of a wall.</p>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-10">
      <table class="text-sm w-full min-w-[740px]">
        <thead>
          <tr class="text-left text-stone-500 border-b border-stone-200">
            <th class="pb-3 pr-5">Model</th>
            <th class="pb-3 pr-5">Listed room range</th>
            <th class="pb-3 pr-5">Listed stone amount</th>
            <th class="pb-3 pr-5">Firewood loading</th>
            <th class="pb-3">Project fit</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-stone-700">
          <tr class="border-b border-stone-100">
            <td class="py-3 pr-5 font-semibold">Harvia M3</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-5">212-459 ft3</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-5">66.2 lb</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-5">Inside sauna</td>
            <td class="py-3">Compact, conventional layout</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-stone-100">
            <td class="py-3 pr-5 font-semibold">HUUM HIVE Flow Mini</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-5">212-494 ft3</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-5">231 lb</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-5">Inside sauna</td>
            <td class="py-3">High stone mass and open-frame design</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-3 pr-5 font-semibold">Harvia Legend 240 SL</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-5">353-848 ft3</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-5">441 lb</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-5">Through-wall extension</td>
            <td class="py-3">Larger room with external loading plan</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <PlannerCTA
      source="wood_heater_guide_above_models"
      heading="Plan the room and chimney before choosing a stove"
      description="Build a project brief with finished dimensions, uninsulated surfaces, loading location, chimney path, budget, and installation needs."
    />

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 mt-10 text-stone-900">Harvia M3: compact, in-room loading</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">Harvia lists the M3, item WKM3, as a 16.5 kW floor stove for sauna rooms from 212 to 459 cubic feet. It measures 15.35 inches wide, 16.93 inches deep, and 27.95 inches high, with a listed stone amount of 66.2 pounds.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-5">This format is the simplest of the three when the fire can be tended inside the sauna and the exact manual's clearances work. The current retailer listing says the stones are required and sold separately. Treat the chimney, protective bedding or sheath, stones, and installation as part of the purchase scope.</p>
    <SelectSaunasButton href={harviaM3Url} label="View current Harvia M3 listing" ctaPosition="harvia_m3_model" />

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 mt-10 text-stone-900">HUUM HIVE Flow Mini: high stone mass in a compact range</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">HUUM lists the HIVE Flow Mini at 8.5 kW for sauna rooms from 212 to 494 cubic feet. It holds about 231 pounds of stones and accepts firewood up to roughly 11.8 inches long. Its current North American product data lists a 4.49-inch flue diameter.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-5">The main tradeoff is visible in the package weight and room plan. The large stone quantity adds thermal mass, but it also adds cost, floor load, handling, and guard considerations. Confirm every clearance dimension from the US manual because a compact stove body does not mean a compact total safety envelope.</p>
    <SelectSaunasButton href={huumFlowMiniUrl} label="View current HIVE Flow Mini listing" ctaPosition="huum_flow_mini_model" />

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 mt-10 text-stone-900">Harvia Legend 240 SL: external loading for a larger room</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">Harvia lists the Legend 240 SL, item WKLE20SLM, as a 21 kW stove for 353 to 848 cubic feet. The SL fire-chamber extension lets the user load wood from another room or outside the sauna. The stove holds 441 pounds of stones and is substantially larger and heavier than the M3.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-5">This is a project-specific format, not an automatic upgrade. The wall penetration, loading-side fire protection, chimney, floor support, stone handling, and clearances all need to be resolved before purchase. Use it when the room and operating plan genuinely benefit from external loading.</p>
    <SelectSaunasButton href={harviaLegendUrl} label="View current Legend 240 SL listing" ctaPosition="harvia_legend_model" />

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 mt-10 text-stone-900">The six checks that decide the purchase</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-3 text-stone-700 mb-8">
      <li><strong>Calculated room:</strong> measure finished volume and apply the selected manufacturer's adjustment for glass, masonry, log walls, and other uninsulated surfaces.</li>
      <li><strong>Local acceptance:</strong> confirm the exact stove, chimney, listing or certification, permit, inspection, and solid-fuel rules with the authority having jurisdiction.</li>
      <li><strong>Clearance envelope:</strong> lay out the stove, door swing, protective surfaces, safety rail, benches, and service access using the current manual.</li>
      <li><strong>Chimney system:</strong> match connector and chimney components to the stove manual, building, roof, and local code. Do not assemble a system from generic diameter advice.</li>
      <li><strong>Combustion air and ventilation:</strong> coordinate both with the heater manual and the sauna design. A sauna exhaust plan is not automatically a complete combustion-air plan.</li>
      <li><strong>Complete package:</strong> price the stove, stones, chimney, flashings, protective bedding and walls, guard, freight, labor, permits, and inspection.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-5 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Do not rely on these shortcuts</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-stone-700">
        <li><strong>&ldquo;Bigger is safer.&rdquo;</strong> An oversized stove can create its own comfort, clearance, and operating problems.</li>
        <li><strong>&ldquo;The stove price is the project price.&rdquo;</strong> Required chimney, stone, protection, freight, and labor can materially change the total.</li>
        <li><strong>&ldquo;All wood stoves use the same clearances.&rdquo;</strong> Clearances are model-specific and can change with approved protective accessories.</li>
        <li><strong>&ldquo;No electricity means no permit.&rdquo;</strong> Solid-fuel appliances, chimneys, wall penetrations, and structures may still require local approval.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-stone-900">FAQ</h2>
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">What is the best wood-burning sauna heater?</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-700">There is no universal winner. The M3 suits a compact conventional layout, the HIVE Flow Mini emphasizes stone mass and design, and the Legend 240 SL serves a larger external-loading plan. The room calculation and installation constraints decide.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">How do I size a wood-burning sauna heater?</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-700">Calculate the finished room volume, include the manufacturer's adjustment for uninsulated surfaces, and use the exact current manual. Do not replace that process with a universal shortcut.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">Does the stove include the chimney and stones?</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-700">Often it does not. Get an itemized package that identifies every required component, freight charge, installation task, and warranty boundary.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-stone-200 pt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Primary sources</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-600">
        <li><a href="https://www.harvia.com/en-US/products/WKM3/m3-black" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Harvia M3, item WKM3</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://huumsauna.com/products/hive-flow-wood-burning-stove/" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">HUUM HIVE Flow product data and US manual</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.harvia.com/en-US/products/WKLE20SLM/legend-240-sl-black" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Harvia Legend 240 SL, item WKLE20SLM</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.harvia.com/en/ideas-and-trends/products/how-do-you-choose-the-right-wood-burning-heater/" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Harvia wood-heater selection guidance</a></li>
        <li><a href={harviaM3Url} rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Current authorized-retailer Harvia M3 listing</a></li>
        <li><a href={huumFlowMiniUrl} rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Current authorized-retailer HIVE Flow Mini listing</a></li>
        <li><a href={harviaLegendUrl} rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Current authorized-retailer Legend 240 SL listing</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-4">Specifications, package contents, availability, pricing, and local requirements can change. Recheck the exact model, current manual, and local approval path before purchase.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-6 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Continue planning</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/guides/wood-burning-sauna/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Check wood-stove, chimney, fuel, and maintenance readiness</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/best-sauna-heater/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Choose between electric and wood heat</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/sauna-heater-sizing-guide/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Organize heater-sizing inputs</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/sauna-ventilation/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Plan sauna ventilation</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/best-electric-sauna-heaters/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Compare current electric-heater formats</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
